{
	title: 'Preserve hosted search evidence in model replay',
	spec: 'Provider-hosted tools remain visible in subsequent model input as a user-side Hal note containing their name, exact input and complete stored output, including failure status, at the next safe user-message boundary after the round that ran them. Replay never puts them in assistant messages, never executes them and never emits foreign provider-native calls. This replaces the display-only replay-dropping rule in a0z. Existing histories need no migration. Offline tests cover recorded provider searches and search failures through replay and provider request mapping.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Root cause: a0z preserved hosted tools for display but explicitly dropped them from provider replay. After an ordinary tool exchange the model retained its search claims while losing the recorded evidence, encouraging repeated searches and contradictory corrections. Replay now converts hosted blocks to labeled assistant text with exact input, stored output and failure status. This applies to both providers and existing records without new schema or client changes. Recorded SSE fixtures exercise the next request through both provider mappers; a separate failure case keeps the complete stored error.',
		'Invariant: hosted tool evidence never appears in assistant messages. Replayed as assistant text ("Provider executed web_search: ..."), Opus 5.5 copied the format and wrote fake searches with invented sources instead of calling the tool (session 49-woo, 19 Nov). Records already holding such fake text are left as they are.'
	],
	needs: ['a0z'],
	foldInto: ['a0z']
}
